  "description": "NEMXOW crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H82 Cu2 N6 O24 Tb4,C1 H4 O1,C1 H2 Cl2,8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.358-3.919 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.92-113.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C98H86Cl2Cu2Tb4N6O25.",
